# The six variables compose.yaml needs, by name only. Their values are private and never go in this repo: they
# live in the Compose helper (in Portainer, the stack's environment variables) or in a .env file beside
# compose.yaml on the machine that runs it. The address, the port, the folder and the topic names may also be
# kept in the vault. The hashes and the tokens never are: the hashes live only in the helper, the tokens only in
# the helper and the Spark's root-only header files, and the vault records where (website/how-to/ntfy.md,
# "The values").
#
# A value holding a `$`, as every bcrypt hash does, is single-quoted, or Compose reads `$` and the letters after it
# as a variable and drops them: NTFY_AUTH_USERS='...'. Portainer writes each variable to a file Compose reads the
# same way, so it takes the same quotes.
NTFY_BASE_URL=<http://NAS-TAILNET-NAME:PORT, ntfy's address as the phone and the Spark reach it>
NTFY_AUTH_USERS=<each user as name:bcrypt-hash:user, comma-separated, single-quoted>
NTFY_AUTH_ACCESS=<each grant as user:topic:permission, comma-separated>
NTFY_AUTH_TOKENS=<each token as user:token, comma-separated>
NTFY_DATA_DIR=<the folder on the NAS that keeps ntfy's databases>
NTFY_PORT=<the NAS's port for ntfy, published to the container's 80>
